# Round 154: recursion that never names itself. `step` is only ever called
# through `dispatch` (a callback-capable builtin), so the call graph has no
# direct edge step -> step; the walk adds an edge from every function that
# makes an opaque call to every function whose name is taken as a value,
# which closes the cycle and brackets step. The VM's cap fires at the same
# depth: one frame per function invocation, the builtin itself has none.
define step(n) as:
    return dispatch of [step, [n + 1]]
print of "start"
print of (step of 0)
print of "unreachable"
